 "documents": {
  "attachments": [
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "Meridian Mutual Insurance\nCertificate of Insurance\n\nWe certify that a policy of event public liability insurance has been issued as follows.\n\nPolicy: PL-827221\nInsured: Clocktower Merchants' Guild\nEvent covered: Clocktower Spring Dash Half Marathon\nLocation of event: Old Quay\nCover starts: 2027-08-27\nCover ends: 2027-08-29\nLimit of indemnity: $2,000,000 any one event\n\nSigned on behalf of the insurer, 2027-04-30\nCertificate reference RQ-94588\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Medical cover for the Clocktower Spring Dash Half Marathon, Saturday 28 August 2027\n\nFrom Anita Bose, Event Secretary, Clocktower Merchants' Guild\n\nThe race is a half marathon with 150 runners and starts at 09:00. We expect a crew from Lifeline Event Medics on the day, though we have nothing in writing yet.\n\nFirst aid\nWe'll have 3 first aid posts, at the start, the finish and halfway, with 12 trained first aiders between them, so nobody on the course is more than about a kilometre and a half from help. We also have two first aiders on bikes, carrying defibrillators.\n\nHeat, cold and water\nThere's water every 2.5 km. We look at the forecast two days before and again two hours before. Over 28 degrees we start earlier or cut the course, and over 32 degrees we call it off. If it's cold or wet, we have foil blankets and a warm tent at the finish.\n\nIf someone needs hospital\nThe nearest emergency department is at Port Halden General Hospital, 9 km from the finish. We've walked the route out from the pick-up point at the boathouse with the first aiders, and we've told the hospital the date and how many are coming.\n\nStaying in touch\nEveryone at a post and both bike first aiders has a radio on our medical channel, with phones as backup. Calls for an ambulance go through our medical lead, who tells the crew which barrier to come to.\n\nWho's responsible\nOur medical lead is Carl Jensen, a registered paramedic, who'll be there from an hour before the start until the last runner is in and has the final word on pulling any runner out.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "Clocktower Spring Dash Half Marathon - race notes\nClocktower Merchants' Guild / contact Anita Bose 555-0155\nSaturday 28 August 2027, gun 09:00, course closes 12:30\nhalf marathon (21k), approx 150 entered\n\nROUTE\nFerry Park ring path then Gardens Loop. no roads, no closures. finish the rowing club\n\nWIDTHS\nFerry Park ring path 10m, open ground beside. Gardens Loop 10m thru parkland, grass both sides. start wide on grass\n\nOTHER\nnumbers from the boathouse 1hr before. chip timing. water on course. results online same day\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "Hello,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nHere is our application for the Clocktower Spring Dash Half Marathon, Saturday 28 August 2027. 150 runners, half marathon, off at 09:00, around Old Quay. I've attached insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt. We have also lined up Lifeline Event Medics for the day.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nThanks,\nAnita\n\nAnita Bose, Clocktower Merchants' Guild\n555-0155\n",
